296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Alongside this technical journey was a very different kind of experience, one that shaped how systems needed to work when people are under pressure. Having lived through instability, recovery, and rebuilding from the edge, Jonathan developed a deep understanding of how people behave when things break down. How decisions slow under stress, how information gets lost, and how easily systems fail when they rely too heavily on human consistency. That experience changed the way systems were designed. It became clear that when people are overwhelmed, systems need to step in, carry the load, and maintain stability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
